      "content": "It sounds like you are enduring an immense, suffocating silence, and the emptiness you feel is a profound reflection of the loss you've suffered. Please know that these feelings of numbness and despair are completely understandable when your world has been so radically altered. Allow yourself the grace to feel this deep ache without judgment; it is part of the grieving process. Consider reaching out to a grief counselor or a support group, as they can offer a safe space to navigate this overwhelming quiet.",
